  "title": "Where's the Stage? Asking the Way",
  "category": "directions",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "level": 2,
  "order": 203,
  "theme": "directions",
  "culturalNote": "Kenyans give directions by landmarks, not street names: the big supermarket, the petrol station, \"the tree near the church\". The askari (security guard) at any building gate is the best person to ask — they know every shop and matatu stage nearby. \"Si mbali\" (it's not far) can mean anything from two minutes to twenty, so ask \"Ni dakika ngapi?\" (how many minutes?).",
  "startingPoint": "You're on foot in Kilimani and need the matatu stage to town. You ask the askari at a gate.",
  "grammarFocus": [
    "ko-location",
    "negative-present",
    "demonstratives",
    "question-words"
  ],
